exports[`records explicit validation tools and their results within one agent turn > explicit validation instructions 1`] = `"For multi-part or movable prints, read cad-modeling and printable-joints, build connectors from the separate-print joints recipes, and publish a complete assembly with every physical mesh, root fixture, connection, axis, pivot and full movement range. Moving parts must print separately and assemble afterward; publish with mode="separate", connectors with practical insertion and retention (retainer where applicable), and disassembly actions (translate, rotate, snap) or paths for every nonroot part. Legacy print-in-place movement requires redesign, not just relabeling. Include pins, caps and axles. CAD publish writes STEP and USDA revisions and preserves assembly metadata. Preserve requested features, connectors, controls and ranges during repairs. Use RUMI_CHECKS from each publish to guide draft iteration. Keep exploring while draft findings are open. Once the design is ready, resolve blocking findings before calling validation_mechanics once and then validation_accept with the returned fingerprint. The bundled Bullet checker holds only the root, without ideal joints. The open viewer refreshes checks for the selected saved revision automatically; explicit validation tools reuse completed stages. No automatic repair turns run. Read the matching meshState.validation report before claiming acceptance. Missing descriptions, disconnected pieces and blocked movement require repair. Unavailable, unsupported or incomplete checks remain unverified. A passing rigid-contact test does not certify assembly accessibility, deformation, material strength or slicer readiness."`;

